<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  <title>We’ve got it — Balance Bridge Financial</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/portal.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/signup.css">
  <link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  <% if (it.signedIn) { %>
  <!-- Signed in: continue straight into the wizard. The page still renders
       identically for everyone, so the response to POST /start reveals nothing
       about whether the email already had an account. -->
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;url=/onboarding">
  <% } %>
</head>
<body class="start">
<header class="start-top">
  <a class="brand" href="/login">
    <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 25h24" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M6 21c3-8 17-8 20 0" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M10 21v4M22 21v4" stroke="#10B981" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
    <span class="brand-word">Balance Bridge <span>FINANCIAL</span></span>
  </a>
  <a class="quiet" href="/login">Sign in</a>
</header>

<main class="done-wrap">
  <div class="mark" aria-hidden="true">✓</div>
  <h1>We’ve got it</h1>
  <p>
    Your books review has started. Check your email — everything you need to pick
    up from here is in it, including the link back into your portal.
  </p>
  <p>
    Next up is a short onboarding wizard. Seven small sections, saved as you go,
    and you can stop halfway and come back tomorrow without losing anything.
  </p>

  <a class="btn-go" href="/onboarding">Continue to onboarding</a>

  <ul class="next-list">
    <li><strong>Sections A to C unlock a real quote</strong> — the legal basics, what you want us doing, and which accounts we would reconcile.</li>
    <li><strong>We never ask for full account numbers or banking passwords.</strong> Last four digits is all we need.</li>
    <li><strong>A person reads it within one business day</strong> and comes back with what we found and a fixed monthly price.</li>
  </ul>
</main>

<footer class="start-foot">
  Balance Bridge Financial · <a href="/login">Sign in</a>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
